  "__readme": "Allowlist for scripts/check-visibility-vocab.ts. Every entry needs a justification: WHY the claim is provable there, or the tracking id (FOUND_DEFECTS.md D106b) for its removal. Delete an entry in the same change that fixes its surface \u2014 that is what re-arms the guard. Never allowlist a NEW write path that sends the retired 'shared'/'private' spellings to the server. Entries match by file, and by line +/-2 when line is set. An entry that suppresses NOTHING is reported as [STALE] by the checker and must be deleted \u2014 a file-level entry blinds the WHOLE file, so a new violation there would never fire. NOTE: D105 is RULED (Arman 2026-07-28) \u2014 'internal' is the correct default and stays; never propose flipping visibility defaults. These surfaces are therefore UNBLOCKED work, not blocked work.",
  "retiredSpelling": [
    {
      "file": "app/(dev)/demos/cloud-files-debug/CloudFilesDebugClient.tsx",
      "justification": "Dev-only debug surface that deliberately exercises legacy spellings to inspect server normalization; read-only, never a write path.",
      "date": "2026-08-08"
    },
    {
      "file": "features/structured-lists/StructuredListManagerV2.tsx",
      "justification": "D106b surface. Its union is a per-domain dialect ('private|authenticated|public') that may mirror the structured-lists table's own enum \u2014 check that table's real column before rewriting. UNBLOCKED (D105 ruled).",
      "date": "2026-08-08"
    },
    {
      "file": "features/user-lists/types.ts",
      "justification": "Per-domain dialect on user_lists ('public|authenticated|private'). Killing it requires a DB enum migration, so it is a deliberate DB change, not a rename \u2014 see FOUND_DEFECTS.md D106b.",
      "date": "2026-08-08"
    }
